--- Message Type Help ---
{
  "envelope": {
    "subject": {
      "use": "notUsed",
      "forms": [],
      "description": "The sales order line is named in data (documentType, documentNo and lineNo, or systemId); subject is not read."
    },
    "dataRequired": true,
    "version": "1.0",
    "contentType": "text/json"
  },
  "target": [
    {
      "source": "data.documentType + data.documentNo + data.lineNo",
      "form": "document type, document no. and line no.",
      "description": "The sales order line, by order number and line number."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.systemId",
      "form": "guid",
      "description": "The sales order line, by its SystemId."
    }
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "documentType",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Order. Only sales order lines can be auto-reserved. Send it with documentNo and lineNo, or send systemId instead."
    },
    {
      "name": "documentNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The sales order number."
    },
    {
      "name": "lineNo",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The line number on the sales order."
    },
    {
      "name": "systemId",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The SystemId of the sales line. Do not send the document keys with it."
    },
    {
      "name": "quantity",
      "type": "number",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The quantity to reserve, in the unit of measure of the line. Optional. Defaults to the outstanding quantity that is not yet reserved, and is capped at it."
    }
  ],
  "response": {
    "contentType": "text/json",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "status",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Success when the line is reserved as asked, or was already fully reserved."
      },
      {
        "name": "documentType",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Always Order."
      },
      {
        "name": "documentNo",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The sales order number."
      },
      {
        "name": "lineNo",
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "The line number on the sales order."
      },
      {
        "name": "systemId",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The SystemId of the sales line."
      },
      {
        "name": "itemNo",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The item number of the line."
      },
      {
        "name": "reserved",
        "type": "decimal",
        "description": "The quantity this call reserved, in the unit of measure of the line."
      },
      {
        "name": "reservedQuantity",
        "type": "decimal",
        "description": "The total quantity reserved on the line after the call, in the unit of measure of the line."
      },
      {
        "name": "outstandingQuantity",
        "type": "decimal",
        "description": "The outstanding quantity of the line, in the unit of measure of the line."
      },
      {
        "name": "fullyReserved",
        "type": "boolean",
        "description": "True when the whole outstanding quantity of the line is reserved."
      },
      {
        "name": "entries",
        "type": "array",
        "description": "One row per reservation entry this call made on the demand side; empty when nothing was reserved.",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "entryNo",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The reservation entry number."
          },
          {
            "name": "itemNo",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The item number of the entry."
          },
          {
            "name": "quantity",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The quantity of the entry; negative on the demand side."
          },
          {
            "name": "quantityBase",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The quantity of the entry in the base unit of measure."
          },
          {
            "name": "shipmentDate",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The shipment date of the entry in YYYY-MM-DD form; blank when there is none."
          },
          {
            "name": "supplyType",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The table number of the supply, left out when the supply side cannot be read."
          },
          {
            "name": "supplyTypeName",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The name of that table, left out with supplyType."
          },
          {
            "name": "supplySubtype",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The subtype of the supply, left out with supplyType."
          },
          {
            "name": "supplyNo",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The document or batch of the supply, left out with supplyType."
          },
          {
            "name": "supplyLineNo",
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The line or entry number of the supply, left out with supplyType."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "when": "A required key is missing.",
      "fix": "Send documentType, documentNo and lineNo, or systemId."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "when": "A key has the wrong JSON type.",
      "fix": "Send lineNo as an integer, quantity as a number and systemId as a GUID."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "documentType is not Order, quantity is zero or less, or the Reservations domain is turned off.",
      "fix": "Send documentType Order and a quantity greater than zero, or turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page."
    },
    {
      "code": "UnknownParameter",
      "when": "The request contains a key this type does not read.",
      "fix": "Remove the unknown key. Allowed keys are documentType, documentNo, lineNo, systemId and quantity."
    },
    {
      "code": "ConflictingIdentifiers",
      "when": "systemId was sent together with document keys.",
      "fix": "Send systemId or the document keys, not both."
    },
    {
      "code": "RecordNotFound",
      "when": "No sales line matches the identifiers.",
      "fix": "Check the document and line no."
    },
    {
      "code": "PreconditionFailed",
      "when": "The item or the line has Reserve set to Never, or the line cannot be reserved: it is not an item line on a sales order, the item is not an inventory item, it is a drop shipment or special order, it has no shipment date, or nothing is outstanding.",
      "fix": "Change the item's Reserve setting or reserve manually."
    },
    {
      "code": "LinesSkipped",
      "when": "Only part of the quantity could be reserved. The partial reservation is rolled back. Nothing is written.",
      "fix": "Read Inventory.Reservation.Get for what was reserved."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "when": "The caller cannot change reservation entries or read sales lines and items.",
      "fix": "Assign the Bifrost \"Full Access\" permission set (extended by Inventory write permissions) and a Business Central permission set that can change these tables."
    },
    {
      "code": "BusinessCentralError",
      "error": "The native reservation error text.",
      "when": "Business Central refuses the reservation while it runs; the answer carries its text.",
      "fix": "Read the error text and correct the line or the supply it names."
    }
  ],
  "effect": {
    "effect": "write",
    "changes": "Creates reservation entries that tie the sales order line to supply that Business Central picks. The reservation is all or nothing: when only part of the requested quantity can be reserved, nothing is kept. Nothing is posted.",
    "idempotent": false,
    "permissionSet": "the Bifrost \"Full Access\" permission set",
    "preconditions": [
      "The Reservations domain is turned on in Inventory Setup.",
      "The line is an item line on a sales order with a shipment date and an outstanding quantity, and Reserve is not Never."
    ],
    "writes": true,
    "posts": false
  },
  "metering": {
    "chargeable": true,
    "chargedAs": "message"
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reservation.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Read the reservations that exist on the line."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reservation.Cancel",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Cancel a reservation entry."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.OrderTracking.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Read which supply is tracked against the line."
    }
  ],
  "workflow": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Reservation.AutoReserve",
        "purpose": "Reserve the sales order line; all or nothing, so a partial reservation answers LinesSkipped."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Reservation.Get",
        "purpose": "Read the reservation entries the line now has."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.OrderTracking.Get",
        "purpose": "Read which supply is tracked against the line."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Reservation.Cancel",
        "purpose": "Cancel a reservation by its entryNo when it is no longer wanted."
      }
    ]
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Reserve a sales order line from inventory",
      "request": {
        "type": "Inventory.Reservation.AutoReserve",
        "data": {
          "documentType": "Order",
          "documentNo": "101005",
          "lineNo": 10000
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "documentType": "Order",
        "documentNo": "101005",
        "lineNo": 10000,
        "systemId": "6f1c1d2e-0000-0000-0000-000000000011",
        "itemNo": "1000",
        "reserved": 2,
        "reservedQuantity": 2,
        "outstandingQuantity": 2,
        "fullyReserved": true,
        "entries": [
          {
            "entryNo": 120,
            "itemNo": "1000",
            "quantity": -2,
            "quantityBase": -2,
            "shipmentDate": "2026-10-20",
            "supplyType": 32,
            "supplyTypeName": "Item Ledger Entry",
            "supplySubtype": 0,
            "supplyNo": "",
            "supplyLineNo": 345
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "overview": "Reserves one sales order line from available supply. Business Central chooses the supply, as the Auto Reserve action on the Reservation page does. Identify the line with documentType, documentNo and lineNo, or with systemId.",
  "notes": "quantity is optional. Without it the call reserves the outstanding quantity that is not reserved yet. reserved is the quantity this call reserved. fullyReserved is true when the whole outstanding quantity of the line is reserved. A line that is already fully reserved answers Success with reserved 0, fullyReserved true and no entries. When only part of the requested quantity can be reserved, the call answers LinesSkipped and keeps nothing: all or nothing. The call runs in its own transaction and does not post."
}

## Errors and warnings
An error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.
When a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.
Request values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.
Request values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `"1234.56"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.
Answers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.
Both success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.
`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {"type":"Memory.User.Set","strict":true,"data":{"memory":"test","memry":"typo"}} is refused.
`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.
Feature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.
A message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.
`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is "no concurrent lock on the same records"; `nextStep` is "Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed." Bifrost does not retry automatically. Other platform errors, including uncaught queue-path errors, remain `BusinessCentralError`.
Codes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.
